    <plot x="10" y="170" height="200" width="390" display="Share of waste handled illegally" xAxis="month" yAxis="share" xMin="0.0" xMax="120.0" yMin="0.0" yMax="0.15" autoPlotX="true" autoPlotY="true" legend="false">
      <setup></setup>
      <update></update>
      <pen display="illegal share" interval="1.0" mode="0" color="-16777216" legend="true">
        <setup></setup>
        <update>plot illegal-share-this-month</update>
      </pen>
    </plot>
  </widgets>
  <info><![CDATA[## WHAT IS IT?

A NetLogo port of a Python prototype: an agent-based model of organised waste crime in Sweden, built for an international research group. See README.md and PROJECT_LOG.md in the repository for the model description, the evidence base and the labelling of every parameter value.

The model is not calibrated and not validated. Results are outcomes under stated assumptions, not estimates of reality.

## HOW TO USE IT

Choose a scenario and a random seed, press setup, then go (or "run to end"). Parameters are read from data/parameters.csv and scenarios from data/scenarios.csv, both generated from the Python project's configuration files. To change a value, edit the CSV (or the YAML in the Python project and re-export).

The BehaviorSpace experiment "regression" runs every scenario with seeds 1 to 30 and reports the same metrics as the Python model, for comparison.
]]></info>
